":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["elasticsearch","java","search-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":25807,"open_issues":5586,"watchers":76300,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/49249","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/49249","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/49249.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/49249.patch","merged_at":"2019-11-21T08:08:32Z"},"body":"fix force stopping transform if indexer state hasn't been written and/or is set to STOPPED. In certain situations the transform could not be stopped, which means the task could not be removed. Introduces improved abstraction in order to better test state handling in future.\r\n\r\nfixes #48957 \r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n\r\n- this turned into a large refactoring and due to upstream changes in code formating produced a lot of formating changes. I therefore put the formating and simple changes into the 1st commit, the [2nd commit](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/commit/45d6715981878f35d95a5723e0943996852f67cc) contains the important parts.\r\n- I had to create a holder class for transform config manager due to problems with service injection. For future enhancements I moved all transform services into the TransformServices holder\r\n\r\n**Reviewers: please start with the 2nd commit, the 1st has only cosmetic changes**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/49249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/49249/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2818656736,"node_id":"M